# The page object of the seed package.
#
# WHAT IT IS FOR ON THIS BRANCH
#
# Both instances run EXT:bootstrap_package 15, which delivers its theme twice:
# as the site set "bootstrap-package/full" and as the static template
# "Configuration/TypoScript/" it registers with addStaticFile(). Every tree of
# the instances is therefore themed. The "/" tree of "core-13" gets the theme
# through the site set, its "/legacy/" tree and the one tree of "core-12"
# through the static template their root "sys_template" record names.
#
# Those records name this static template first and the theme right after it,
# so in those trees the theme replaces this page object. Of this file only the
# "config" flags "contentObjectExceptionHandler" and "disablePrefixComment"
# stay in effect there, the theme sets neither. It is the smallest page object
# that puts the content of a page on the page, and it renders where the theme
# is not installed: the functional suite loads the packages of this repository
# and not "bk2k/bootstrap-package", which only the instances require. There the
# theme entry resolves to nothing, and without this page object the seeded
# pages would render nothing at all.
#
# It is shipped twice, as this static template folder, named by the
# "include_static_file" of the root "sys_template" records, and as the site set
# "fgtclb/academics-dev-site-page-object", whose "setup.typoscript" imports this
# file. The set is what "LegacyDeliveryTest" puts in the place of the theme on
# the "/" side, so that inside the harness both trees are rendered by the same
# text and a difference the test reports is a difference in what the academic
# extensions deliver.

page = PAGE
page {
    typeNum = 0

    10 = COA
    10 {
        10 = TEXT
        10.data = page:title
        10.wrap = <h1>|</h1>

        20 < styles.content.get
    }

    meta.viewport = width=device-width, initial-scale=1
}

config {
    # Absolute paths, so a link of the mirrored tree differs from its original by
    # the "/legacy" segment and by nothing else.
    absRefPrefix = /
    # An exception in a content element is something to see, not something to
    # replace with a box that renders the same on both sides of a comparison.
    contentObjectExceptionHandler = 0
    disablePrefixComment = 1
    headerComment = Delivered by the static template of EXT:academics_dev_site.
}
